        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Updates for Safari TP 255]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31024</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/31024"/>
        <updated>2026-11-02T15:54:21.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/349114?u=1185d4fc45f5ff4c4a592b30a4dd2bb5cd1b7128&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">The <a href="https://collector.openwebdocs.org/" rel="nofollow">https://collector.openwebdocs.org/</a> project (v10.21.1) found new features shipping in Safari Technical Preview 255 on macOS 27 which was released last week. Currently, the collector covers about 90% of BCD, so the following list might not be exhaustive.</p>
<p dir="auto">Release notes: <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/18482/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-255/" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/blog/18482/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-255/</a></p>
<p dir="auto">New (<strong>bold</strong>) and updated keys:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>api.SVGTextPathElement.side</li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-block-end-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-block-start-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-bottom-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-inline-end-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-inline-start-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-left-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-right-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.border-top-radius</strong></li>
<li><strong>css.properties.continue.collapse</strong></li>
<li>css.properties.interpolate-size</li>
<li>css.properties.interpolate-size.allow-keywords</li>
<li>css.properties.interpolate-size.numeric-only</li>
</ul>
<p dir="auto">Notes:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li>The STP 255 release notes don't mention border-*-radius side shorthands and interpolate-size, but they were mentioned for STP 254: <a href="https://webkit.org/blog/18420/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-254/" rel="nofollow">https://webkit.org/blog/18420/release-notes-for-safari-technology-preview-254/</a>. For BCD, the result is the same, it gets marked as "preview" now.</li>
</ul>]]></content>
