    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Firefox 160: WebTransport.exportKeyingMaterial() outputLength parameter]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30999</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/30999"/>
        <updated>2026-11-03T15:01:58.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5368500?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><p dir="auto">Firefox 160 makes the <code class="notranslate">context</code> parameter of <code class="notranslate">exportKeyingMaterial()</code> required and adds the required <code class="notranslate">outputLength</code> parameter, matching the spec in <a href="https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2079306" rel="nofollow">https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2079306</a>.</p>
<p dir="auto">Firefox 155-159 implemented an earlier draft: <code class="notranslate">context</code> was optional and the output was fixed at 32 bytes.</p>
<p dir="auto">What I've done is added a subfeature <code class="notranslate">outputLength_parameter</code> for the new parameter.</p>
<p dir="auto">I've marked FF155-159 support as partial_implementation with a note that attempts to capture this. Note that it isn't "really" partial  - it was correct (I think) at the point it was submitted. However its only been around for 5 releases so this feels a bit like a significant spec completion and hence grounds to indicate the first version as partial. Happy to remove that if you want.</p>
<p dir="auto">Related docs work can be tracked in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="6044207520" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46281" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/content/issues/46281/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/content/issues/46281">mdn/content#46281</a></p>]]></content>
